Subject: [PATCH] mtk: ccif: defer periodic traffic reports during CPU idle

The CCIF traffic timer queues diagnostic work that prints port and packet
counters and rearms the same timer. It is not the modem health watchdog
or the packet-delivery path. Let that diagnostic timer defer during CPU
idle instead of waking a CPU solely to queue a status dump.

Retain the callback, workqueue, nominal interval, log counters, timer
start/stop and all hardware wake/recovery paths. Reports may arrive later
when idle; active packet handling does not depend on the report deadline.

This targets the Rodin vendor CCCI module, not the common boot image.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_ccif.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_ccif.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_ccif.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_ccif.c
@@ -1811,7 +1811,7 @@
 
 	timer_setup(&ccif_ctrl->traffic_monitor,
-		md_ccif_traffic_monitor_func, 0);
+		    md_ccif_traffic_monitor_func, TIMER_DEFERRABLE);
 	INIT_WORK(&ccif_ctrl->traffic_info.traffic_work_struct,
 		md_ccif_traffic_work_func);
 
 	ccif_ctrl->channel_id = 0;
